# Implementation Plan - MTG Set Names Fix

This plan outlines the steps to replace the 3-letter Magic set codes (e.g., "LEA", "M21") with their full descriptive names (e.g., "Limited Edition Alpha", "Core Set 2021") and fix the "Unknown Set" label in the admin inventory.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This fix requires connecting to the [Scryfall API](https://scryfall.com/docs/api) once to fetch the official set list. Only a single request is needed to sync all 600+ historical sets.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Database & Model Update

We need to ensure the `mtg_sets` table is fully populated and that the model is joining correctly. I will add a synchronization method to pull data from Scryfall.

#### [MODIFY] [Mtg_model.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/models/Mtg_model.php)
- Add `sync_sets_from_api($sets_data)`: A helper to loop through Scryfall data and `INSERT ... ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE` the `mtg_sets` table.
- Ensure `get_mtg_inventory_by_set` and other methods consistently join with `mtg_sets`.

### 2. Admin Controller Integration

I will add a new AJAX endpoint to trigger the synchronization.

#### [MODIFY] [Admin.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/controllers/Admin.php)
- Add `sync_mtg_sets_ajax()`: This will perform the `curl` request to `https://api.scryfall.com/sets`, parse the JSON, and call the model to save the names.

### 3. UI Update (Admin Console)

Add a "Sync" button to let the admin refresh the names if new sets are added in the future.

#### [MODIFY] [mtg_inventory.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/views/admin/mtg_inventory.php)
- Add a "**🔄 Sync Set Names**" button in the controls header.
- Add JavaScript logic to handle the sync request and reload the page on success.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- I will verify the Scryfall API response format matches our expected structure.

### Manual Verification
- Navigate to **Admin > Magic Inventory**.
- Verify that the "Select Set" dropdown now shows full names like "Alpha" instead of "LEA".
- Verify that the "Unknown Set" badge in the table is replaced by the actual set name.
